  "notes": "London psych-soul, \"the lane's most orchestral and most guitar-driven modern entry\". The drum block encodes a subtraction the entry states directly: \"dry, tape-compressed live kit — kick on 1 and 3, snare on 2&4 with a short damped decay, tambourine and handclaps, and a deliberate absence of high-frequency hat detail\". That absence is the lowest hat fill density in this batch (0.05) with an `openHat.prob` of 0.03 — the hats are effectively withheld — over a kick anchored literally on 1 and 3. \"Long drumless intros are structural (his best-known track opens with roughly four minutes of no backbeat)\", which is the 8-to-32-bar intro in the arrangement. The band is the catalogue's own 65–125 and the keys are the named F major, E minor, A minor, G minor and B♭ minor. Harmony is \"folk-soul with modal cadences (`i–VII–VI`, `i–iv`, `I–IV–I–V`), long pedal passages, and orchestral reharmonisation on repeats rather than modulation\" — all three families are the entry's own, and the long pedal is the 4-to-16-beat chord duration. Melody is \"mid-tenor, warm, low note-density, hymn-like in contour, doubled by strings or choir on the chorus\": near-total stepwise motion, an arch-weighted contour, a very high chord-tone bias and a `sustain_pad` counter for the strings. Bass is \"round and simple, moving in 8ths on chord roots with occasional octave drops… often enters a full section after the guitar\". ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are all drum probabilities and velocities and every melody number; the research marks the drum-tone description as inference.",
